Before you do anything else, get unburdened.  Go back to one of your
stashes and put all those unidentified potions in it for a start.
Likewise food; just keep 2-3 rations with you at all times and keep
the rest in your stash.

Then do Sokoban.

What you do after that depends on what you get and whether you already
have magic resistance.  If you get the amulet, or if you don't have
magic resistance already, you'll want to do the quest right away. You
may need to kick sinks to get a foocubus to bring you to XL 14. Do
that at as high a dungeon level as possible so the other monsters will
be weak, and clear the level before kicking.

If you do have magic resistance, you might want to go down to Medusa's
level (if you haven't seen it already, you're close) and see if you
can find a shield of reflection in the Perseus statue. (Archaeologists
take an alignment penalty for destroying the statues on that level,
but it's worth it for reflection).  Whether you find a shield or not,
the quest should probably be your next stop, but keep an eye out for
reflection.

Oh, and no, a potion of levitation isn't something you should ever
rely on to cross more than a few squares of water.  Either find
boots of levitation or water walking, or freeze the water with
a wand of cold and watch out for anything that might have a wand
of fire. But that comes after you have MR and reflection.  The
Perseus statue might have (cursed) boots of levitation.


